      },
      "text": "START\nPatient reports back, neck or upper-back pain.\nAlready established: the pain seems musculoskeletal (spine, joints, discs, muscles or nerves). Stage 1 still re-checks the organs that most often disguise themselves as back or neck pain."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6415",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6415",
        "x": "11680",
        "y": "528",
        "width": "520",
        "height": "222",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Q0 · Where is the main pain?\nASK: “Point with one finger to where it hurts the most, then show me everywhere else you feel it.”\nDO: draw it on a body chart — the drawing is reused in Stage 2 and at every re-test."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7334",
      "type": "connector",
