      "text": "G-Q0&gt;G-A0N"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:6431",
      "type": "shape-with-text",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "1:6431",
        "x": "11680",
        "y": "1245",
        "width": "520",
        "height": "349",
        "name": "ROUNDED_RECTANGLE"
      },
      "text": "Use MOVEMENT to decide\nAsk them to bend, arch and twist the low back, then turn, tip and nod the head and lift both arms. The region whose movement reproduces the familiar pain is the source.\nMid-back pain that changes with breathing, twisting the chest or arm movement → NECK & UPPER BACK pathway. Pain that changes with bending and arching the low back → LOW BACK pathway.\nMid-back (thoracic) pain is itself a warning sign for fracture, cancer and TB — run the Stage 1 checks carefully."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "rWECNSFkKrOGuJkRPvsQdP:1:7350",
